      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A post office was established by at least 1908, serving as a key hub in the isolated mountain area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/mayhill_new_mexico",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The community lies at the confluence of James Canyon and the Rio Penasco, a perennial stream that supports riparian zones with willows and cottonwoods.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/mayhill_new_mexico",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "At elevations between 6,575 and 6,700 feet, Mayhill enjoys cool summers with highs around 80–83°F and cold winters dropping to 20–25°F, with annual snowfall averaging 14–23 inches.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/mayhill_new_mexico",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The pine-dominated forest of Mayhill, part of the Sacramento Mountains “sky island,” supports unique biodiversity, including ponderosa pine, Douglas fir, and endemic species adapted to the elevation gradient.",
